# Everything text is stored and checked out LF, on every platform.
#
# Without this, a clone made on Windows with core.autocrlf=true gets CRLF in its
# working tree. The content is unchanged, but the bytes are not — and run
# manifests record digests of these files to prove two runs used the same
# benchmark. `content_digest` in src/ym07/digests.py now normalises line endings
# so a stray CRLF can no longer split one benchmark into two, but keeping the
# working tree consistent in the first place is the cheaper half of the fix.
* text=auto eol=lf
# Binary — never touch these.
*.pdf binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
# Raw course material is stored exactly as received. Two files in it were
# committed with CRLF, and normalising them would rewrite course material for
# the sake of line endings nobody reads.
corpus/raw/** -text
*.safetensors filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.pt filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.pth filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
